<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix: Case Studies</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the Appendix, we present 5 representative real cases to demonstrate the advantage of <span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OptScale</span> in terms of both performance and token consumption over BoN.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Case 1 (See Table <a href="#A1.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Case Studies ‣ Probabilistic Optimality for Inference-time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) is a representative of very easy questions. Both BoN and <span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OptScale</span> start with a correct answer in the first round. However, BoN introduces an overwhelmingly additional wasted rounds because of the fixed N required. And the model is distracted by the small number of completions with wrong answers it generates across. Overall, BoN wasted 42 completions as the final selected answer actually comes from Completion 18. In contrast, <span id="A1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OptScale</span> has successfully identified that this is a very easy question, and stops reasoning at the 10th Completion, resulting in significant token consumption reduction of 80.13%.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Case 2 (See Table <a href="#A1.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Case Studies ‣ Probabilistic Optimality for Inference-time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) is a representative of difficult questions. Both BoN and <span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OptScale</span> hit the correct answer for the first time on Completion 4. During the entire process, lots of different answers are generated, of course, among which only 1 answer is correct. <span id="A1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OptScale</span> successfully recognizes the proper level of difficulty for this question and stops reasoning at Completion 22 through the dynamic adjustment mechanism. However, BoN introduces additional rounds because of its nature of generating a fixed number of rounds for each question, the model seems to be confused by various wrong answers generated during the excess sampled generations. Eventually, such confusion results in BoN choosing the wrong answer in the end. <span id="A1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OptScale</span> achieves a significant reduction of token consumption of 65.14% while better utilizing this scaled compute for achieving the final correctness for this question.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Case 3 (See Table <a href="#A1.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Case Studies ‣ Probabilistic Optimality for Inference-time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) is a representative of questions with middle-level difficulty, typically on the secondary school Mathematics Competition level. Both BoN and <span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OptScale</span> hit the correct answer at Completion 1. Most of the time, the model could generate the correct answer with minor wrong answer distractions. However, BoN introduces an additional round, making it waste all the generations from Completion 14 to Completion 60 as no higher score is assigned (the final generation BoN chooses is at Completion 13). <span id="A1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OptScale</span> terminates on Completion 19, significantly reducing token consumption by 69.47% by correctly evaluating how much inference-time compute to allocate for this question. Both methods answer this question correctly in the end.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Case 4 (See Table <a href="#A1.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Case Studies ‣ Probabilistic Optimality for Inference-time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) is another representative of a difficult question. Both BoN and <span id="A1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OptScale</span> hit the correct answer at Completion 3 for the first time. Similar to Case 2, some of the generated answers are wrong across the different sampled completions. BoN introduces additional completions, which creates confusion for itself as more wrong answers come in during the later phase of sampled generations. Such confusion eventually causes BoN to select the wrong answer in the end. <span id="A1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OptScale</span> decisively determines to terminate on Completion 14, significantly reducing token consumption by 76.07% and obtaining the correct final answer.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Case 5 (See Table <a href="#A1.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Case Studies ‣ Probabilistic Optimality for Inference-time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) is a representative of questions of upper-middle level difficulty. Both BoN and <span id="A1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OptScale</span> hit the correct answer at Completion 2 for the first time. The majority of the answers are correct. BoN introduces additional completions to answer this question correctly, while <span id="A1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OptScale</span> successfully evaluates this question and decides to terminate on Completion 6. This proves to be clever, as the final chosen Completion is also Completion 6, achieving completely no waste on inference-time compute scaling. This helps <span id="A1.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OptScale</span> significantly reduce token consumption by 90.04% and obtain the correct final answer.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A1.T2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="A1.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Case 1 (Dataset: GSM8K, Backbone Model: Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct).</span></figcaption>
<table id="A1.T2.5" class="ltx_tabular">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A1.T2.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T2.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" colspan="3">
<span id="A1.T2.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:331.2pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T2.5.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">Question:<span id="A1.T2.5.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <span id="A1.T2.5.1.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">A robe takes 2 bolts of blue fiber and half that much white fiber. How many bolts in total does it take?</span></span></span></span>
</span></th></tr>
<tr id="A1.T2.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T2.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T2.5.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">N</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="A1.T2.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T2.5.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Best-of-N (BoN)</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="A1.T2.5.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T2.5.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">OptScale</span></span>
</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A1.T2.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T2.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T2.5.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion 1</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T2.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T2.5.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">… # Step 3: Calculate the total amount of fiber required.</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">The final answer is: <math id="A1.T2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">3</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{3}</annotation></semantics></math> 
<br class="ltx_break">(Already hit the correct answer)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T2.5.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Same as BoN</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T2.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T2.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T2.5.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion 2</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T2.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T2.5.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">… total_fiber_needed = blue_fiber_needed + white_fiber_needed = 4 + 2 = 6 …</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">The final answer is: <math id="A1.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">6</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{6}</annotation></semantics></math> 
<br class="ltx_break">(Move to the wrong answer)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T2.5.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Same as BoN</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T2.5.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T2.5.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T2.5.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion 3-9</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T2.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">(The final answer is kept at the correct answer “3”.)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T2.5.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Same as BoN</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T2.5.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T2.5.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T2.5.6.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion 10</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T2.5.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">(BoN keeps on generating new completions as it doesn’t know when to stop.)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T2.5.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.6.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.6.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Reaches the optimal number of sampled completions. <span id="A1.T2.5.6.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OptScale</span> terminates here with the correct answer 3.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T2.5.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T2.5.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.7.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T2.5.7.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion 22</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T2.5.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.7.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.7.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">(BoN jumps back to wrong answer “6”.)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T2.5.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T2.5.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T2.5.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.8.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.8.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T2.5.8.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion 43</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T2.5.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.8.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.8.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T2.5.8.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">… # Step 3: Calculate the total amount of fiber required. Total fiber required is 2 bolts of blue fiber + 1/2 * white fiber.</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T2.5.8.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"># Step 4: Simplify the expression. To simplify the expression, we can convert 2 bolts of blue fiber to 2 * 2 = 4 bolts, since 2 bolts * 2 = 4. Then the expression becomes 4 + 1/2 * white fiber.</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">The final answer is: <math id="A1.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{4.25}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">4.25</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{4.25}</annotation></semantics></math> 
<br class="ltx_break">(BoN has a wrong understanding of this easy question and moves to a wrong answer “4.25”.)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T2.5.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T2.5.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T2.5.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.9.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.9.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T2.5.9.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion 60</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T2.5.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.9.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.9.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">(BoN eventually stops as required when N=60 and gives the correct answer 3 after choosing the answer with the highest verifier score.)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T2.5.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T2.5.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T2.5.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.10.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.10.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T2.5.10.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Token Consumption</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T2.5.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.10.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.10.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">12,103</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T2.5.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.10.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.10.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">2,485</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T2.5.11" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T2.5.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bbbb ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.11.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.11.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T2.5.11.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Correctness</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T2.5.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bbbb ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.11.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.11.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T2.5.11.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">Yes (✓)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T2.5.11.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bbbb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T2.5.11.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.5.11.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T2.5.11.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">Yes (✓)</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A1.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="A1.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Case 2 (Dataset: AIME24, Backbone Model: Deepseek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B).</span></figcaption>
<table id="A1.T3.5" class="ltx_tabular">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A1.T3.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T3.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" colspan="3">
<span id="A1.T3.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:331.2pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">Question:<span id="A1.T3.5.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <span id="A1.T3.5.1.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">A list of positive integers has the following properties:
<math id="A1.T3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bullet" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathcolor="#0000FF">∙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bullet</annotation></semantics></math> The sum of the items in the list is <math id="A1.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathcolor="#0000FF">30</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">30</annotation></semantics></math>.
<math id="A1.T3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bullet" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathcolor="#0000FF">∙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bullet</annotation></semantics></math> The unique mode of the list is <math id="A1.T3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathcolor="#0000FF">9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9</annotation></semantics></math>.
<math id="A1.T3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bullet" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathcolor="#0000FF">∙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bullet</annotation></semantics></math> The median of the list is a positive integer that does not appear in the list itself.
Find the sum of the squares of all the items in the list.</span></span></span></span>
</span></th></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T3.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">N</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="A1.T3.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Best-of-N (BoN)</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="A1.T3.5.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">OptScale</span></span>
</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A1.T3.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T3.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion 4</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T3.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">… After several attempts and checking for valid configurations, we find that the list <math id="A1.T3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[5,7,9,9]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[5,7,9,9]</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies all conditions:</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.3.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">- The sum is <math id="A1.T3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5+7+9+9=30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5+7+9+9=30</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.3.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">- The mode is 9, appearing twice, more than any other number.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.3.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">- The median is <math id="A1.T3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{7+9}{2}=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{7+9}{2}=8</annotation></semantics></math>, which is not in the list.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.3.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Finally, we calculate the sum of the squares of all the items:</span>

<br class="ltx_break"></span>
<span id="A1.T3.5.3.2.1.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.T3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.T3.5.3.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> + <math id="A1.T3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>7</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> + <math id="A1.T3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> + <math id="A1.T3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> = 25 + 49 + 81 + 81 = 236</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.3.2.1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Thus, the sum of the squares of all the items in the list is <math id="A1.T3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\boxed{236}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">236</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\boxed{236}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>

<br class="ltx_break">(The first time the models hit the correct answer)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T3.5.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Same as BoN</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T3.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion 6</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T3.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">… Constructing the list:</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.4.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">- The mode is 9, which must appear at least twice.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.4.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">- The median is the average of the second and third numbers, which is an integer not present in the list.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.4.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We find that the list [5, 7, 9, 9] satisfies all conditions: …</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.4.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">- Calculating the sum of the squares of the items in the list:</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.4.2.1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">- <math id="A1.T3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5^{2}+7^{2}+9^{2}+9^{2}=25+49+81+81=236" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>7</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>25</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>49</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>81</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>81</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>236</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5^{2}+7^{2}+9^{2}+9^{2}=25+49+81+81=236</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.4.2.1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Thus, the sum of the squares of all the items in the list is <math id="A1.T3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\boxed{236}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">236</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\boxed{236}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">(Hit the correct answer again)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T3.5.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Same as BoN</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.5.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T3.5.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion 8</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T3.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">… After several attempts and considerations, we find that the list can be structured as follows:</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.5.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">- The list has 6 elements, as this is the smallest odd number that allows the median to be a positive integer not in the list.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.5.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">- The list is sorted and includes two 9s, which are the mode.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.5.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">- The remaining four numbers must sum to 12 and be distinct positive integers different from 9.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.5.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The valid list found is:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1,2,4,5,9,9]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1,2,4,5,9,9]</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.T3.5.5.2.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.5.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This list satisfies all conditions:</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.5.2.1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">- The sum is <math id="A1.T3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+2+4+5+9+9=30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+2+4+5+9+9=30</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.5.2.1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">- The mode is 9, appearing twice.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.5.2.1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">- The median is the average of the 3rd and 4th numbers, which is <math id="A1.T3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{5+9}{2}=7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{5+9}{2}=7</annotation></semantics></math>, a positive integer not in the list.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.5.2.1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Finally, we calculate the sum of the squares of all the items:</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.5.2.1.2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> <math id="A1.T3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> + <math id="A1.T3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> + <math id="A1.T3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> + <math id="A1.T3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> + <math id="A1.T3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> + <math id="A1.T3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> = 1 + 4 + 16 + 25 + 81 + 81 = 208 </span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.5.2.1.2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Thus, the sum of the squares of all the items in the list is:</span> <math id="A1.T3.m24" class="ltx_Math ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" display="block" intent=":literal"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">208</mn></math>

<br class="ltx_break">(Previously, all wrong answers couldn’t be extracted as numbers. This is the first numerical wrong answer.)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T3.5.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Same as BoN</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.5.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T3.5.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.6.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion 22</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T3.5.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">… Wait, n=7: two 9s, sum contributed by 9s=18. Sum remaining=12.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.6.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">So, five numbers, each positive integer, sum=12, each number appears at most once.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.6.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Minimal sum for five distinct positive integers:1+2+3+4+5=15&gt;12. So, impossible.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.6.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">n=6: two 9s, sum=18. Sum remaining=12.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.6.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">n=6: four numbers, sum=12, each number appears at most once.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.6.2.1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">So, minimal sum for four distinct positive integers:1+2+3+4</span>

<br class="ltx_break">(BoN continues generation.)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T3.5.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.6.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.6.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">(<span id="A1.T3.5.6.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OptScale</span> terminates. Based on verifier scoring, it chooses the answer from Iteration 6 as the final answer, which is correct.)</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.5.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T3.5.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.7.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.7.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion 26-35</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T3.5.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.7.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.7.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.7.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We need to find the sum of the squares of all the items in the list.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.7.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">First, we consider the number of elements in the list, denoted as <math id="A1.T3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. Since 9 is the unique mode, it must appear at least twice. We also need to ensure the median is an integer not present in the list.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.7.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">After analyzing different possible values for <math id="A1.T3.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, we find that <math id="A1.T3.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=6</annotation></semantics></math> works. The list must have three 9s and three 1s to satisfy all conditions:</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.7.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">- The sum of the list is <math id="A1.T3.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+1+1+9+9+9=30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+1+1+9+9+9=30</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.7.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">- The mode is 9, which appears three times, more than any other number.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.7.2.1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">- The median is the average of the third and fourth numbers, which is <math id="A1.T3.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1+9}{2}=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1+9}{2}=5</annotation></semantics></math>, an integer not present in the list.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.7.2.1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The sum of the squares of the items in the list is calculated as follows:</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.7.2.1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> <math id="A1.T3.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> + <math id="A1.T3.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> + <math id="A1.T3.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> + <math id="A1.T3.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> + <math id="A1.T3.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> + <math id="A1.T3.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> = 1 + 1 + 1 + 81 + 81 + 81 = 246 </span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.7.2.1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Thus, the sum of the squares of all the items in the list is <math id="A1.T3.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\boxed{246}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">246</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\boxed{246}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>

<br class="ltx_break">(BoN keeps struggling between right and wrong answers. Correct answers appear several times, while wrong answers, such as 201 and 246, also appear.)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T3.5.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.5.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T3.5.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.8.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.8.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.8.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion 37</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T3.5.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.8.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.8.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.8.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Final Answer</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.8.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The sum of the squares of all the items in the list is <math id="A1.T3.m37" class="ltx_Math ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" display="block" intent=":literal"><mn>208</mn></math>.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.8.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">&lt;/think&gt;</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.8.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given the properties of the list of positive integers:</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.8.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">1. The sum of the items is 30.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.8.2.1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">2. The unique mode is 9.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.8.2.1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">3. The median is a positive integer that does not appear in the list.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.8.2.1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We need to find the sum of the squares of all the items in the list.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.8.2.1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">First, we note that 9 is the unique mode, so it must appear at least twice. The sum of the list is 30, so the remaining sum after accounting for two 9s is 12.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.8.2.1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Considering the median, since the median must be a positive integer not in the list, the list must have an even number of elements. We explore the case with 6 elements (n=6), as it is the smallest even number that allows the median to be a non-integer.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.8.2.1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For n=6, the list has two 9s and four other distinct numbers summing to 12. The possible sets of four distinct numbers are [1, 2, 3, 6] and [1, 2, 4, 5]. The set [1, 2, 3, 6] results in a median that is an integer, which is invalid. The set [1, 2, 4, 5] results in a median that is not in the list.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.8.2.1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Thus, the list is [1, 2, 4, 5, 9, 9]. The sum of the squares of these numbers is calculated as follows:</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.8.2.1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">[</span>
<math id="A1.T3.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.T3.5.8.2.1.1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> + <math id="A1.T3.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> + <math id="A1.T3.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> + <math id="A1.T3.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> + <math id="A1.T3.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> + <math id="A1.T3.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> = 1 + 4 + 16 + 25 + 81 + 81 = 208</span>
<span id="A1.T3.5.8.2.1.1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">]</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.8.2.1.1.16" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Therefore, the sum of the squares of all the items in the list is <math id="A1.T3.m44" class="ltx_Math ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" display="block" intent=":literal"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">208</mn></math>.</span>

<br class="ltx_break">(BoN generates the wrong answer 208 again.)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T3.5.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.5.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T3.5.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.9.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.9.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.9.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion 38-59</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T3.5.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.9.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.9.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.9.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">… After considering all possibilities, the only valid list is for <math id="A1.T3.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=4</annotation></semantics></math> with the sum of squares calculated as follows:</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.9.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">- The list is [5, 7, 9, 9].</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.9.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">- The sum of the squares is <math id="A1.T3.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5^{2}+7^{2}+9^{2}+9^{2}=25+49+81+81=236" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>7</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>25</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>49</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>81</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>81</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>236</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5^{2}+7^{2}+9^{2}+9^{2}=25+49+81+81=236</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.9.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Thus, the sum of the squares of all the items in the list is <math id="A1.T3.m47" class="ltx_Math ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" display="block" intent=":literal"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">236</mn></math>.</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">(During this period, BoN either generates the correct answer "236" or "None".)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T3.5.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.5.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T3.5.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.10.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.10.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.10.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion 60</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T3.5.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.10.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.10.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.10.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">After testing various configurations, we find that the list [5, 7, 9, 9] satisfies all conditions:</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.10.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">- The sum is 5 + 7 + 9 + 9 = 30.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.10.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">- The mode is 9, which appears twice.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.10.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">- The median is (7 + 9)/2 = 8, which is not in the list.</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.10.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The sum of the squares of the items in the list is calculated as follows:</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><math id="A1.T3.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.T3.5.10.2.1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> + <math id="A1.T3.m49" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>7</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> + <math id="A1.T3.m50" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> + <math id="A1.T3.m51" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> = 25 + 49 + 81 + 81 = 256</span>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T3.5.10.2.1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Thus, the sum of the squares of all the items in the list is <math id="A1.T3.m52" class="ltx_Math ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" display="block" intent=":literal"><mn>256</mn></math>.</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">(BoN eventually stops as required when N=60. In Completion 60, the model generates the wrong answer "256". Unfortunately, BoN chooses the answer in Completion 37 based on PRM scoring, which is the wrong answer 208. Despite spending so many tokens, BoN fails to give the correct answer.)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T3.5.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.5.11" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T3.5.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.11.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.11.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.11.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Token Consumption</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T3.5.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.11.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.11.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">544,797</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T3.5.11.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.11.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.11.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">189,908</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.5.12" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T3.5.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bbbb ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.12.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.12.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.12.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Correctness</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T3.5.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bbbb ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.12.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.12.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.12.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">No (✗)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T3.5.12.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bbbb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T3.5.12.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A1.T3.5.12.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T3.5.12.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">Yes (✓)</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A1.T4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="A1.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Case 3 (Dataset: AMC23, Backbone Model: Deepseek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B).</span></figcaption>
<table id="A1.T4.5" class="ltx_tabular">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A1.T4.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T4.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" colspan="3">
<span id="A1.T4.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:331.2pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.5.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">Question:<span id="A1.T4.5.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <span id="A1.T4.5.1.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">For how many ordered pairs <math id="A1.T4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathcolor="#0000FF">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathcolor="#0000FF">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathcolor="#0000FF">b</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,b)</annotation></semantics></math> of integers does the polynomial <math id="A1.T4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{3}+ax^{2}+bx+6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathcolor="#0000FF">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathcolor="#0000FF">3</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathcolor="#0000FF">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathcolor="#0000FF">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathcolor="#0000FF">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathcolor="#0000FF">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathcolor="#0000FF">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathcolor="#0000FF">b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathcolor="#0000FF">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathcolor="#0000FF">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathcolor="#0000FF">6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{3}+ax^{2}+bx+6</annotation></semantics></math> have <math id="A1.T4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathcolor="#0000FF">3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> distinct integer roots?</span></span></span></span>
</span></th></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T4.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.5.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">N</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="A1.T4.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.5.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Best-of-N (BoN)</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="A1.T4.5.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.5.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">OptScale</span></span>
</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A1.T4.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T4.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.5.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion 1</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:345.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.5.3.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">To determine the number of ordered pairs <math id="A1.T4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,b)</annotation></semantics></math> of integers such that the polynomial <math id="A1.T4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{3}+ax^{2}+bx+6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{3}+ax^{2}+bx+6</annotation></semantics></math> has three distinct integer roots, we use the Rational Root Theorem and factorization.
<br class="ltx_break">The polynomial must have integer roots, which are divisors of the constant term 6. The possible roots are <math id="A1.T4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 1,\pm 2,\pm 3,\pm 6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 1,\pm 2,\pm 3,\pm 6</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">The polynomial can be expressed as <math id="A1.T4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x-r)(x-s)(x-t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x-r)(x-s)(x-t)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.T4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r,s,t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r,s,t</annotation></semantics></math> are distinct integers. Expanding this gives:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{3}-(r+s+t)x^{2}+(rs+rt+st)x-rst" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{3}-(r+s+t)x^{2}+(rs+rt+st)x-rst</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.T4.5.3.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.5.3.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Comparing coefficients:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=-(r+s+t),\quad b=rs+rt+st,\quad rst=-6" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=-(r+s+t),\quad b=rs+rt+st,\quad rst=-6</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.T4.5.3.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.5.3.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Each valid triple leads to a unique ordered pair <math id="A1.T4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,b)</annotation></semantics></math>. The valid sets are:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<span id="A1.Ex4X"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(-1,2,3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(-1,2,3)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rightarrow(-4,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rightarrow(-4,1)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex4Xa"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(-2,1,3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(-2,1,3)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rightarrow(-2,-5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rightarrow(-2,-5)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex4Xb"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(-3,1,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(-3,1,2)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rightarrow(0,-7)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rightarrow(0,-7)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex4Xc"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(-1,-2,-3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(-1,-2,-3)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rightarrow(6,11)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rightarrow(6,11)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex4Xd"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(6,1,-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(6,1,-1)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4Xd.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rightarrow(-6,-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rightarrow(-6,-1)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.T4.5.3.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.5.3.2.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Thus, the number of ordered pairs <math id="A1.T4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,b)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.T4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn>5</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{5}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Same as BoN</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T4.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.5.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion 2-8</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.5.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The correct answer is repeated in Iteration 3. Some answers in other iterations were not completed before reaching the max token limit.</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Same as BoN</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.5.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T4.5.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.5.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion 9</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:345.0pt;"><span id="A1.T4.5.5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We find all sets of three distinct integers whose product is <math id="A1.T4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-6</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">Possible sets: (-1,2,3), (-2,1,3), (-3,1,2), (-1,-2,-3).
<br class="ltx_break">Each gives a unique <math id="A1.T4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,b)</annotation></semantics></math>, except only 4 are counted. Therefore the answer is <math id="A1.T4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn>4</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{4}</annotation></semantics></math>. (Incorrect)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Same as BoN</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.5.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T4.5.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.5.6.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion 10-18</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:345.0pt;"><span id="A1.T4.5.6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Most completions correctly derive the answer <math id="A1.T4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn>5</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{5}</annotation></semantics></math>, though Completion 10 and Completion 16 repeat wrong answer <math id="A1.T4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn>4</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{4}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.6.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.6.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Same as BoN</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.5.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T4.5.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.7.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.5.7.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion 19</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.7.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.7.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:345.0pt;"><span id="A1.T4.5.7.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Correct pairs: (-6, -1), (-4, 1), (-2, -5), (0, -7), (6, 11).
<br class="ltx_break">Hence, total is <math id="A1.T4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn>5</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{5}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.7.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.7.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.5.7.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OptScale</span> selects Completion 13 with the correct answer.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.5.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T4.5.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.8.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.8.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.5.8.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion 19-59</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.8.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.8.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.5.8.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Most completions repeat correct answer <math id="A1.T4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn>5</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{5}</annotation></semantics></math>. Completion 33 repeats wrong answer <math id="A1.T4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn>4</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{4}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.5.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T4.5.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.9.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.9.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.5.9.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion 60</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.9.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.9.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:345.0pt;"><span id="A1.T4.5.9.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Final correct answer <math id="A1.T4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn>5</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{5}</annotation></semantics></math> is confirmed.
<br class="ltx_break">Best PRM scoring still from Completion 13.</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.5.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T4.5.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.10.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.10.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.5.10.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Token Consumption</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.10.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.10.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">534,991</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.10.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.10.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">163,311</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.5.11" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T4.5.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.11.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.11.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.5.11.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Correctness</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.11.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.11.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.5.11.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">Yes (✓)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.11.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.5.11.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.5.11.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.5.11.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">Yes (✓)</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A1.T5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 5</span>: </span><span id="A1.T5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Case 4 (Dataset: AIME25, Backbone Model: Deepseek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B).</span></figcaption>
<table id="A1.T5.5" class="ltx_tabular">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A1.T5.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T5.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" colspan="3">
<span id="A1.T5.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:331.2pt;">
<span id="A1.T5.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T5.5.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">Question:<span id="A1.T5.5.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <span id="A1.T5.5.1.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">Sixteen chairs are arranged in a row. Eight people each select a chair in which to sit so that no person sits next to two other people. Let <math id="A1.T5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathcolor="#0000FF">N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of subsets of 16 chairs that could be selected. Find the remainder when <math id="A1.T5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" mathcolor="#0000FF">N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is divided by 1000.</span></span></span></span>
</span></th></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T5.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T5.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T5.5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T5.5.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">N</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="A1.T5.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T5.5.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T5.5.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T5.5.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Best-of-N (BoN)</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="A1.T5.5.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T5.5.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A1.T5.5.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T5.5.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">OptScale</span></span>
</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A1.T5.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T5.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T5.5.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T5.5.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion 3</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T5.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T5.5.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T5.5.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:345.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T5.5.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">… To solve this problem, we model it by selecting 8 chairs such that no three selected chairs are adjacent. We can think of this as placing 8 ones among 16 positions such that no three ones are consecutive.</span>
<span id="A1.T5.5.3.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_p">We break this into cases based on the number of blocks (runs) of 1s:</span>
<span id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<span id="A1.Ex5X"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{For }m=4:" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>For </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{For }m=4:</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\binom{4}{4}\cdot\binom{9}{4}=126" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>4</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>9</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>126</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\binom{4}{4}\cdot\binom{9}{4}=126</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex5Xa"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle m=5:" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle m=5:</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\binom{5}{3}\cdot\binom{9}{5}=1260" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>9</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1260</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\binom{5}{3}\cdot\binom{9}{5}=1260</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex5Xb"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle m=6:" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle m=6:</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\binom{6}{2}\cdot\binom{9}{6}=1260" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>6</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>9</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1260</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\binom{6}{2}\cdot\binom{9}{6}=1260</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex5Xc"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle m=7:" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle m=7:</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\binom{7}{1}\cdot\binom{9}{7}=252" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>7</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>9</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>252</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\binom{7}{1}\cdot\binom{9}{7}=252</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex5Xd"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle m=8:" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle m=8:</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5Xd.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\binom{8}{0}\cdot\binom{9}{8}=9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>8</mn><mn>0</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>9</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\binom{8}{0}\cdot\binom{9}{8}=9</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.T5.5.3.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_p">Total number of valid arrangements:</span>
<span id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="126+1260+1260+252+9=2907" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>126</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1260</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1260</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>252</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2907</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">126+1260+1260+252+9=2907</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.T5.5.3.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_p">Taking modulo 1000:</span>
<span id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2907\mod 1000={\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\boxed{907}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2907</mn><mo>mod</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">907</mn></menclose></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2907\mod 1000={\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\boxed{907}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.T5.5.3.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_p">(Correct)</span>
</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T5.5.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T5.5.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:71.1pt;">
<span id="A1.T5.5.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Same as BoN</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T5.5.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T5.5.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T5.5.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completion 6,7</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T5.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T5.5.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T5.5.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:345.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T5.5.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">… We model the problem as binary strings of length 16 with exactly 8 ones, no three consecutive.</span>
<span id="A1.T5.5.4.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_p">Let each run of 1s be of length 1 or 2. The remaining zeros are distributed between the runs. For each possible number of runs <math id="A1.T5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, compute:</span>
<span id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{r}{8-r}\cdot\binom{9}{r}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>9</mn><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{r}{8-r}\cdot\binom{9}{r}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.T5.5.4.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_p">Summing over <math id="A1.T5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=4</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.T5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math>, we get:
<math id="A1.T5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="126+1260+1260+252+9=2907" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>126</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1260</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1260</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>252</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2907</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">126+1260+1260+252+9=2907</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span id="A1.T5.5.4.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.T5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Rightarrow 2907\mod 1000={\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\boxed{907}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mn>2907</mn><mo>mod</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">907</mn></menclose></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Rightarrow 2907\mod 1000={\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\boxed{907}}</annotation></semantics></math>

<br class="ltx_break">(Correct)</span>
</span>
</span></td>
